From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Filer island paint out of descendant popovers

Paint the owned sidebar/content surfaces and file views. Generic viewport
descendant selectors also match GtkPopoverMenu internals, covering the shared
menu surface with a second, rectangular background. Leave those containers
transparent instead of overriding or recreating the toolkit menu contract.

--- a/src/resources/style.css
+++ b/src/resources/style.css
@@ -300,7 +300,6 @@
   }
 
   .luma-files-window .luma-sidebar-surface,
-  .luma-files-window .luma-sidebar-surface viewport,
   .luma-files-window .luma-sidebar-surface .navigation-sidebar {
     background-color: @luma_content;
     color: @luma_ink;
@@ -345,8 +344,7 @@
 
 
   .luma-files-window .luma-content-surface,
-  .luma-files-window .luma-content-surface .view,
-  .luma-files-window .luma-content-surface viewport {
+  .luma-files-window .luma-content-surface .view {
     background-color: @luma_content;
     color: @luma_ink;
   }
